# Wave T46 (Inglenook kit): domeroof — the GOLD DOME of the Inglenook Contest Hall, worn only by the shipped Contest Hall stamp's tr roof cells (the town sign's own words: 'Contests under the gold dome'). GOLD DOME SEGMENTS: horizontal arc bands of gold with violet shadow seams, offset segment joints and a highlight crest — a dome drawn as tiling. No other fleet roof curves: Heritage's heritageroof is flat teal slate courses, Honeyfield's bloomroof petal scales, Coalseam's ironroof riveted plate. (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T46-INGLENOOK-PLAN.md §5.)
